ation that enumerates each of the eleven rather than a single-phrase grep.","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC6: 'the eleven inline Terraform comments that assert \\'no X published in a period is the healthy steady state\\' are corrected... Verified by grep.'","grep 'healthy steady state' hits only monitoring_88ab.tf:57, monitoring_s5.tf:50, monitoring_s4b.tf:78, monitoring_1fa8.tf:74","monitoring_ws7.tf:48-49 uses 'the probe fails safe' phrasing, not 'healthy steady state'","monitoring_foxterrier.tf:68 and :104 have a bare `treat_missing_data = \"notBreaching\"` with no adjacent justifying comment"],"finding":"AC6 asserts 'the eleven inline Terraform comments that assert \"no X published in a period is the healthy steady state\"' and that this is 'Verified by grep', but a grep for that phrase matches only 4 alarm files (monitoring_88ab.tf:57, monitoring_s5.tf:50, monitoring_s4b.tf:78, monitoring_1fa8.tf:74). mirror_out_of_sync uses different wording ('the probe fails safe', monitoring_ws7.tf:48-49), and both foxterrier alarms (mcp_retire_cap, mcp_mem_abort) carry NO justifying comment beside treat_missing_data at all (monitoring_foxterrier.tf:68,104). The premise that eleven comments carry that assertion is refuted, and AC6's grep-based verification will not find eleven.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4aeb5021abaa92de","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC6","norm_id":"n1da71ac809c0be22","priority":0.8,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer greps for the exact 'healthy steady state' phrase, corrects 4 comments, and marks AC6 done — leaving foxterrier's uncommented alarms and mirror/bridge's differently-worded comments untouched."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Reword AC6 to: 'each of the eleven rebar/host notBreaching alarms either has its inline missing-data rationale corrected or (where none exists, e.g. the foxterrier alarms) gains an accurate one; verified by inspecting each of the eleven resource blocks, not a single-phrase grep.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] AC3: specify the exact else-branch value for mirror_out_of_sync (e.g. publish an alarming datapoint such as 1, NOT 0) so a fetch/REST failure is distinguishable from in-sync, and state that it relies on AC2's evaluation_periods>=3 window to suppress transient-blip flapping.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.1778,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC3: 'mirror_out_of_sync publishes a value on its else branch (fetch/REST failure) rather than publishing nothing'","observability.sh:417-418 comment: 'On a fetch failure we publish NOTHING (the alarm treats missing data as healthy) rather than risk a false alarm from a blip'","observability.sh:425 shows the happy-path values are 0 (in sync) and 1 (drift); a fetch-failure signal must be distinguishable from both to be actionable","Tuning constraint section widens flipped alarms to evaluation_periods >= 3, which is what makes a fetch-failure '1' safe from single-tick flap — but AC3 does not state the else branch must emit that alarming value under that widened window"],"finding":"AC3 says mirror_out_of_sync must 'publish a value on its else branch ... rather than publishing nothing' but does not specify WHICH value, and the choice is mechanism-critical: publishing 0 preserves the fail-open reading (fetch failure looks in-sync), while publishing 1 flaps the alarm on every transient blip — the exact false-alarm risk the existing comment at observability.sh:415-418 was written to avoid. Without pinning the value (and reconciling it with AC2's evaluation-window widening), the implementer can satisfy AC3's literal text while either not fixing the fail-open (publish 0) or introducing chronic flapping (publish 1).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd44df9643c6d155a","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria — AC3","norm_id":"n8b532a78e0bf64ee","priority":0.7778,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer publishes 0 on fetch failure: AC3 passes literally, but a breaching flip now reads a broken Gerrit REST call / git ls-remote as 'in sync' — the fail-open that motivated the ticket persists","Implementer publishes 1 on fetch failure with evaluation_periods=1 not yet widened: a single transient curl timeout pages"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Amend AC3 to require the else branch publish an ALARMING value (e.g. mirror_out_of_sync=1) so a sustained fetch failure crosses the breaching threshold, explicitly paired with the AC2 widening to >=3 periods so a single jittered fetch failure does not page.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] In AC3, state the disposition explicitly: specify that the else branch publishes a threshold-crossing (breaching) value on fetch/REST failure — not 0 — and change the verification to observe a *breaching* datapoint, not merely any datapoint.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T12","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.failure-disposition-contract"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0111,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC3: 'publishes a value on its else branch (fetch/REST failure) rather than publishing nothing, so a breaching flip converts a silent failure into a real signal instead of a noisy one. Verified by inducing a fetch failure and observing a datapoint.'","The other counters publish delta 0 as the healthy value; a 0 on the else branch would not breach.","AC3's verification observes 'a datapoint' not a breaching datapoint."],"finding":"AC3 changes the mirror_out_of_sync fetch/REST-failure path to publish a value instead of nothing, but never states WHICH value the else branch publishes or that it crosses the alarm threshold. If the else branch publishes 0 (matching the healthy steady state), a breaching flip still reads OK on fetch failure and the fail-open gap is not actually closed; only a threshold-crossing value converts the silent failure into a firing signal.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa49a8b54d09ee5ff","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC3","norm_id":"nbccca9376131136b","priority":0.8889,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A live host whose Gerrit REST call or git ls-remote breaks: else branch publishes 0, alarm stays OK, GitHub main drift stays unpaged — the exact fail-open the plan targets."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Have the else branch publish a sentinel value that exceeds the mirror_out_of_sync alarm threshold, and update AC3 verification to assert the alarm transitions to ALARM on induced fetch failure.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify in AC3 that the else-branch datapoint must be a value that CROSSES the alarm threshold (a breaching value, e.g. 1 with threshold 0), not merely 'a value', and verify the induced fetch failure actually drives the alarm to ALARM state.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["T5b","E2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0137,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC3: 'publishes a value on its else branch (fetch/REST failure) rather than publishing nothing, so a breaching flip converts a silent failure into a real signal instead of a noisy one'","Section 1 notes the alarm reads OK when the else branch publishes nothing; but a 0 value under a >0 threshold alarm is equally OK","The publisher pattern elsewhere publishes 0 for healthy periods, so 'a value' is ambiguous vs. a breaching value"],"finding":"AC3 requires mirror_out_of_sync to 'publish a value on its else branch ... rather than publishing nothing', but does not specify that the value must CROSS the alarm threshold (i.e. be a breaching value, not 0). If the else branch publishes 0, the breaching flip still reads 0 as OK and the silent fetch/REST failure remains invisible — defeating the stated purpose of converting a silent failure into a real signal.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fdef751f7808f5dc9","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC3 (Acceptance criteria) and section 1 (mirror_out_of_sync)","norm_id":"n03f113096b7088fa","priority":0.5863,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor implements the else branch to publish 0 (matching the healthy-period convention); the alarm never fires on a real Gerrit REST / git ls-remote failure despite the breaching flip"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Reword AC3 to: 'mirror_out_of_sync publishes a breaching value (above the alarm threshold) on its else branch when the Gerrit REST call or git ls-remote fails, verified by inducing a fetch failure and observing the alarm transition to ALARM.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_cap